1
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:37,039
Here it comes.

2
00:01:37,039 --> 00:01:38,560
You really caught one. It took the bait.

3
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:39,720
It's such a big one.

4
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:41,340
We didn't buy this one.

5
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:42,960
This is a real river fish.

6
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:46,680
It really is quite big. That's amazing.

7
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:48,160
You are amazing, Sister Long.

8
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:49,360
The director is here.

9
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:51,479
President.

10
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:56,759
Thank you for being willing to see me again.

11
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:59,960
Is this case really that important to you?

12
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:04,200
If you withdraw the lawsuit,

13
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,200
the company will arrange for you to fly again

14
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,860
and qualify you for a promotion to chief purser.

15
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:11,490
I never thought of getting promoted this way.

16
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:13,600
I just want fairness.

17
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,680
Why are you so stubborn?

18
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:17,320
Is fairness that important?

19
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:20,200
Are you willing to keep wasting your time here?

20
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:29,720
My client has been very persistent.

21
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:31,840
She just wants a fair result.

22
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,200
Then as her attorney,

23
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,280
to be honest,

24
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,040
I also want to prove to the judge

25
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:37,920
that psychological trauma

26
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,920
is a real wound

27
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:42,280
and shouldn't be ignored.

28
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,480
Lawyer Tian must have told you

29
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:49,400
about the case I appeared in court for him.

30
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,280
It's useless.

31
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:51,840
It's all in vain.

32
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,040
To tell you the truth,

33
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:56,040
I'm very disappointed.

34
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:58,920
Compared to the progress of social civilization and awareness,

35
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,920
the judicial system is lagging too far behind.

36
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:01,560
Yes.

37
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:05,480
Director, I understand your concerns.

38
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:07,680
But we've also done some research.

39
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:08,280
Actually,

40
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:09,280
there are now domestic precedents

41
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:11,280
supporting psychological trauma.

42
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:12,410
What does this mean?

43
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,320
It means times have changed.

44
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:16,040
Although it seems right now

45
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,840
that our efforts are very small,

46
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:20,280
it is only these tiny efforts

47
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,680
that can drive the progress of the times, isn't it?

48
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:24,480
How would we know if we don't try?

49
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:25,480
Director,

50
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:28,200
we must have faith in the law.

51
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:30,890
Faith alone is useless.

52
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:33,140
How can the judge believe just me?

53
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:34,280
I think

54
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:38,360
if we let the court know more about the public's

55
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:40,000
views on this incident,

56
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:42,240
it would be more helpful.

57
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:44,440
What does that mean?

58
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:46,570
Are you going to appear in court or not?

59
00:03:49,079 --> 00:03:51,079
I understand, Director. Thank you.

60
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:53,000
I've said all I have to say.

61
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,079
Young man,

62
00:03:55,079 --> 00:03:55,840
let it go.

63
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:58,900
You didn't catch it to eat?

64
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:14,000
Psychological Trauma Cognitive Questionnaire

65
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,480
For specific cases, there are no right or wrong answers. Please answer based on your true thoughts. Thank you for your support!

66
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:16,160
2. In a confined space, how would you feel if a male stranger suppressed and assaulted you?

67
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:17,560
Excuse me, am I bothering you?

68
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:17,839
Not at all.

69
00:04:17,839 --> 00:04:19,700
Well, I'm doing a questionnaire,

70
00:04:19,839 --> 00:04:20,680
doing this...

71
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,720
Psychological Trauma Cognitive Questionnaire.

72
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,120
Hey handsome, come help us fill out a form.

73
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,560
Sister Pang's Bathhouse is having an event.

74
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,840
Fill out the Psychological Trauma Cognitive Questionnaire,

75
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:31,440
and get a free choice of vinegar, salt, or milk for your scrub.

76
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,160
What are you looking at?

77
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:02,360
I'm not copying. I'm just taking a look.

78
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:05,160
Longnv.

79
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:07,880
I had someone at the market make these today.

80
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:08,840
That's a lot.

81
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:09,840
Thanks for your hard work, Squad Leader.

82
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:10,680
Thank you, Squad Leader.

83
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:11,680
Squad Leader is here too.

84
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:13,840
Beihu, let's grab a bite together. Come on.

85
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:15,160
Let me tell my wife first.

86
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:17,400
Honey, I won't be home for dinner today.

87
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,530
Get some rest early.

88
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,080
Mwah.

89
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,360
Mwah.

90
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:22,200
This is a meme from two years ago.

91
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:24,280
Everything is just a passing cloud.

92
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:31,840
These are the questionnaires we've done over the past few days.

93
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:33,840
If it's not enough, we can continue.

94
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:48,240
What's the suitcase for?

95
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:51,780
Lawyer Li is the airline's lawyer. Of course he's here.

96
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:03,480
Court is now in session.

97
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:06,840
Will the expert assistant please explain

98
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:09,500
what these questionnaires are meant to convey.

99
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:12,480
The questions in the questionnaire include

100
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:15,840
asking respondents to imagine themselves in a confined space,

101
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:19,000
being pinned down and torn at by a strange man.

102
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:21,480
92% of female respondents

103
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,920
and 69% of

104
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,480
male respondents stated

105
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,960
that they would view this behavior

106
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:28,880
as a violent assault and feel fear.

107
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:31,120
Do the appellant's symptoms meet

108
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,159
the diagnostic criteria for Acute Stress Disorder?

109
00:06:33,159 --> 00:06:34,840
Based on the medical records,

110
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,200
I believe they fully meet the criteria.

111
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:40,360
Does the appellee wish to question the expert assistant?

112
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,040
Yes.

113
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,480
Let me make an assumption here.

114
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,480
If I also memorized those

115
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,600
answers that could lead to a diagnosis

116
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,040
of ASD,

117
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,480
and filled them out exactly as they are,

118
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:52,720
would I also be diagnosed

119
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:53,480
with ASD?

120
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,159
Very likely.

121
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:57,480
Dean Zhuge, I would like to ask,

122
00:06:57,720 --> 00:07:00,360
based on Xu Jiayi's questionnaire that you saw,

123
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,480
how likely do you think it is

124
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:04,360
that Xu Jiayi memorized the answers

125
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,040
in advance?

126
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,240
Extremely unlikely.

127
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:08,600
From the details of her handwriting,

128
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:10,120
I can even feel her emotions.

129
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:12,160
How can you prove that Xu Jiayi's

130
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:12,840
ASD

131
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:14,480
was caused by Hu Sheng?

132
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:16,480
Xu Jiayi's symptoms appeared

133
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:18,600
only a few days after the conflict.

134
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:21,240
It corresponds logically in terms of time.

135
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:23,000
Moreover, the infringement occurred

136
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,840
in a confined space like an airplane cabin.

137
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,480
This would further amplify the victim's

138
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:29,480
subjective assessment of the threat and danger.

139
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:32,159
Since you also mentioned subjective assessment,

140
00:07:32,159 --> 00:07:33,240
is it possible

141
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:35,040
that the conflict itself was not enough

142
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,840
to cause much harm to Xu Jiayi,

143
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:37,240
and the reason for her

144
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:38,360
ASD

145
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:40,000
is her own vulnerability?

146
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,850
It is very possible.

147
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,600
Most studies have found that

148
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,480
for ASD,

149
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,120
the incidence rate

150
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:46,480
shows gender differences.

151
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:48,840
The incidence in women is significantly higher than in men.

152
00:07:48,840 --> 00:07:50,240
If you say she is vulnerable,

153
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:51,600
it only further strengthens

154
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:52,720
the connection between her ASD

155
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:54,480
and this conflict.

156
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,040
Our society

157
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:58,120
has always emphasized the rule of law and civilization.

158
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,240
What is the rule of law?

159
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:01,600
The rule of law is to make the weak fearless.

160
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,840
What is civilization?

161
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:05,170
Civilization is to give the weak dignity.

162
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:08,160
Every word you say favors the appellant.

163
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:10,820
Were you hired by them through the back door?

164
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:13,240
Please observe courtroom discipline.

165
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:17,160
Do both parties have anything to add to their final statements?

166
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:17,720
I do.

167
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,240
Regarding this conflict

168
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:22,160
involving my client in the cabin,

169
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:25,160
many people say she is making a fuss over nothing

170
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:26,840
and being overly sensitive.

171
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,840
That's because this trauma

172
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:31,160
is invisible and intangible.

173
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,159
But psychological harm

174
00:08:33,159 --> 00:08:34,679
is also real.

175
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:36,320
It's just that

176
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:39,120
there is no accurate physiological numerical standard

177
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:41,760
to define its existence

178
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:43,400
and severity in the judicial system.

179
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:45,640
resulting in the rights of some patients with mental illness

180
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:47,160
being unprotected.

181
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:50,800
Nowadays, our society pays more attention to

182
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:53,130
mental health and psychological issues.

183
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:55,360
And some domestic courts have already

184
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:57,800
started to recognize psychological trauma.

185
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:59,160
I think our Leyang

186
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:01,800
should keep pace with the times.

187
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:09,800
It's still the same issue.

188
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:12,330
Her symptom is called acute stress disorder.

189
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:13,600
As for the resulting damage,

190
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:15,480
we currently have no way to quantify it.

191
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:16,920
There is no standard for determination.

192
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:18,800
If so, the causal relationship

193
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:20,360
between this result and the appellee's behavior

194
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,360
is hard to determine.

195
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:23,240
Recently,

196
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:24,360
I have carefully studied

197
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:25,800
the materials provided by the appellant.

198
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,240
I think it's enough to prove

199
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:29,360
that the mental damage is not groundless.

200
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,840
I've read those cases.

201
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,700
The materials are very detailed.

202
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,360
But in our region,

203
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:36,610
there has never been such a precedent.

204
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,600
It's a difficult choice to make.

205
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,480
Please be seated.

206
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:56,160
In the case of Xu Jiayi v. Hu Sheng regarding the right to life and health,

207
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:57,620
after trial by this court,

208
00:09:57,840 --> 00:10:01,120
it is determined that Xu Jiayi has suffered psychological injury,

209
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,760
and it has a direct causal relationship

210
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:04,690
with Hu Sheng's extreme behavior.

211
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:06,980
The judgment of this court is as follows.

212
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:09,360
All rise.

213
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:15,440
1. The first-instance civil judgment is revoked.

214
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:18,480
2. Within seven days after this judgment

215
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,080
takes effect, Hu Sheng shall

216
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:22,780
publicly apologize to the plaintiff, Xu Jiayi,

217
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:25,360
and pin it to the top for a week without removal.

218
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:27,760
3. Hu Sheng shall, upon this judgment...

219
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:30,240
Actually, I have a different opinion.

220
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Our practice should keep pace with the times.

221
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:36,480
After all, progress isn't something we wait for,

222
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:38,480
but something we create ourselves.

223
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,840
There's a first time for everything,

224
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,120
and we shouldn't be afraid

225
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,360
to be the first.

226
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:45,720
pay medical expenses of 2,250 yuan.

227
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,600
8,000 yuan for lost wages

228
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:50,480
and 12,000 yuan for mental distress.

229
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:54,600
The case acceptance fees for the first and second instances shall be borne by Hu Sheng.

230
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:57,000
This judgment is final.

231
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:59,240
The court is now adjourned.

232
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:03,840
Let's just order some takeout at the law firm later.

233
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:04,600
Let's get something to eat.

234
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,760
Why order takeout?

235
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,360
I can just show off my cooking skills.

236
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:08,600
You can cook?

237
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:09,200
Leyang God of Cookery.

238
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,120
Guaranteed to win.

239
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:11,650
Is this the result I wanted?

240
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:14,580
The verdict is out. There's nothing I can do.

241
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:19,360
What are you looking at?

242
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:20,120
I see.

243
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:22,360
Mr. Hu, we all know

244
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:23,860
your time is precious.

245
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:25,200
Since everyone is here,

246
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,120
why don't you just apologize?

247
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:29,850
Then we won't have to see each other again, right?

248
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:34,560
You've been making a fuss for so long just for money, haven't you?

249
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:36,360
Fine, I'll add 50,000.

250
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:38,080
Not enough.

251
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:39,840
Then I'll add another 100,000.

252
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,120
Is that enough to cover an apology?

253
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:41,960
No, it's not.

254
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:43,600
We don't want money.

255
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:44,760
We just want an apology.

256
00:11:44,760 --> 00:11:45,960
Isn't that annoying?

257
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:46,840
I just won't apologize.

258
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:47,600
Isn't that annoying?

259
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:49,600
Then just wait for the court to publish the verdict.

260
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:51,360
Let the published verdict be your apology.

261
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,360
You're so ungrateful.

262
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:53,120
Who are you calling ungrateful?

263
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,240
Mr. Hu, let's go.

264
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:54,600
What do you say?

265
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:55,960
Go? Why should we go?

266
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:58,320
A flight attendant

267
00:11:58,320 --> 00:11:59,120
and a lousy lawyer.

268
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:00,840
You wouldn't even see me without this stupid case.

269
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:02,960
You will all pay the price,

270
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:03,360
you know?

271
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:04,360
Mr. Hu.

272
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,360
What price?

273
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:09,520
The price for insult,

274
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:11,960
or the price for threatening others?

275
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,120
This is the court.

276
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:14,120
It's quite convenient.

277
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:15,080
You...

278
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:15,600
Mr. Hu.

279
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:17,360
Stop making a scene.

280
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:18,320
Just apologize.

281
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,440
A wise man knows when to retreat.

282
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:20,960
What? Stop making a scene?

283
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:22,440
Wan Gang.

284
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:33,080
That flight attendant.

285
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:33,840
I'm sorry.

286
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:35,890
What's with your attitude?

287
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:37,360
Are you asking for a napkin?

288
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,690
It's fine, Lawyer Xiao.

289
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:50,060
You can't hurt me anymore.

290
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,440
What are you talking about?

291
00:12:56,440 --> 00:12:57,600
No, you...

292
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:58,480
What are you talking about?

293
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:00,360
I'm the victim in this case.

294
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:02,160
Mr. Hu, stop making a scene. I...

295
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,440
And you.

296
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:05,200
I spent so much money

297
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:06,880
hiring you to represent me,

298
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:08,760
not to lose my case.

299
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:09,360
With that much money,

300
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,600
I'd be better off raising pigs than you.

301
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:11,880
Even pigs are better than you, you know?

302
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:12,740
Say something.

303
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:18,360
I'm done.

304
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:23,840
Wait, Wu Yong.

305
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:26,090
Thanks for your help this time.

306
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:28,840
You really did a great job this time.

307
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:31,840
Lawyer Li knows how to compliment people now,

308
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:33,120
and so directly too.

309
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,120
What do you mean?

310
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:37,120
I've always known how to compliment people.

311
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:37,960
Really?

312
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:38,840
Where are you going? I'll give you a ride.

313
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:39,360
No need.

314
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:42,320
I invited everyone to eat at my law firm.

315
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:44,770
If you're not busy, you can come along.

316
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:46,600
Sure.

317
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:49,840
You're not busy?

318
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:50,520
Not busy.

319
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:53,320
Come to my law firm to eat.

320
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:54,200
I heard you.

321
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:55,600
Let's take my car.

322
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:58,060
I don't feel safe with Little Tiger driving.

323
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,400
Don't you need to read the files?

324
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:03,090
If you're busy, don't force yourself.

325
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:04,900
What are you doing?

326
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:07,460
Didn't we agree to eat at the firm?

327
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:09,880
Sister Long said

328
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:12,040
Lawyer Li is eating with us today.

329
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:13,840
Great. The more, the merrier.

330
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:15,360
No, why is he going?

331
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:16,840
Doesn't he have food at home?

332
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,840
Are there enough chairs at the firm?

333
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:21,370
He's so inconsiderate.

334
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:29,440
Uncle, how come you forgot how to drive?

335
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:37,120
Here's the tableware.

336
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:40,320
Miao.

337
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,120
Go get a new set of bowls and chopsticks.

338
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:43,360
Li Lü is a germaphobe.

339
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:44,320
Understood.

340
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:47,240
Li Lü doesn't look like he can cook.

341
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:48,360
He's very good at it.

342
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:50,600
He's been cooking since he was a kid, and it's delicious.

343
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:52,440
My uncle also said he's been cooking since he was a kid.

344
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,120
Really?

345
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:55,120
Shouldn't we go help?

346
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,840
Is it appropriate to let the two men cook?

347
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:58,600
What's inappropriate about it?

348
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,600
The kitchen should be a man's battlefield.

349
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:02,600
Then let's sit here and wait to eat.

350
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,650
We're exactly three short.

351
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:18,440
What are you looking at?

352
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:19,500
Eat your heart out.

353
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:29,880
Look at this.

354
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:32,250
These dishes are

355
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:35,360
a combination of Chinese and Western styles.

356
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:37,840
I didn't expect Lawyer Li to be so handsome,

357
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:39,480
and his cooking to be so beautiful too.

358
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:40,200
Yes, thank you.

359
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:42,600
Lawyer Li, these dishes are perfect for me.

360
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:43,360
Low oil and low salt,

361
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:44,360
healthy and good for weight loss.

362
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:45,360
Then eat more.

363
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:46,840
Yeah.

364
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:48,360
We're tired after a long day, eating some leaves,

365
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:50,320
and then going back to our cages to sleep at night.

366
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:51,520
What do you mean, leaves?

367
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:53,320
Steak, meat pies.

368
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:54,760
These are all heavy dishes.

369
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:55,080
Well,

370
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,840
come on, let's propose a toast.

371
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:58,360
Um, I want to say something.

372
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:00,360
Everyone has been working so hard for my case

373
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:01,760
for such a long time.

374
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:03,120
I want to toast everyone

375
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:03,600
to thank you all.

376
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:05,359
Jiayi, we should toast you.

377
00:17:05,359 --> 00:17:06,520
To your bravery,

378
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:07,599
and your persistence,

379
00:17:07,599 --> 00:17:09,359
which made this case a success.

380
00:17:09,599 --> 00:17:10,319
Right?

381
00:17:11,359 --> 00:17:11,839
Cheers.

382
00:17:11,839 --> 00:17:12,640
Thank you all.

383
00:17:12,839 --> 00:17:13,599
Cheers.

384
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:14,359
Uncle.

385
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:17,839
Jiayi.

386
00:17:18,319 --> 00:17:20,849
What you said to Hu Sheng at the end was so cool.

387
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:22,119
How did it go again?

388
00:17:23,359 --> 00:17:25,119
"You can't hurt me anymore."

389
00:17:25,119 --> 00:17:26,240
So cool.

390
00:17:26,359 --> 00:17:27,880
Yeah, just that one sentence

391
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,840
broke Hu Sheng's defenses instantly.

392
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,640
His face changed immediately.

393
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:33,360
Winning this case

394
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:34,600
is actually, to me

395
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:35,960
and to Director Zhuge,

396
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:37,600
a great encouragement.

397
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:39,360
I should really thank everyone.

398
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:40,760
Our old monitor is right.

399
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:42,840
With the successful precedent of Jiayi's case,

400
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:44,360
for similar cases in the future,

401
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:45,360
the court will have to take them seriously.

402
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:47,120
Anyway, we did a good thing.

403
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:47,760
Right?

404
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:49,120
Come on, let's have a toast.

405
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:49,960
Come on.

406
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:51,380
We're all good people.

407
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:54,600
Alright, don't be so formal.

408
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:55,660
Let's eat. Come on.

409
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:01,840
What's gotten into you?

410
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:03,300
Laughing like that again.

411
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:05,220
I did a good thing. Don't scold me.

412
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:06,360
Come on.

413
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:07,960
No, Wu Yong.

414
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:10,420
Wu Yong, come back.

415
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:11,960
Serves him right.

416
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:12,880
Look at the bullet comments.

417
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,320
They are all scolding Hu Sheng.

418
00:18:14,320 --> 00:18:14,960
Really?

419
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:16,200
I even posted two.

420
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:18,440
My name is Hu Sheng.

421
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:19,360
I just want to humiliate

422
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:20,120
and hurt others.

423
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:21,360
Everyone, look at the verdict.

424
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:22,360
Lose, lose, lose.

425
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:23,840
The court ruled

426
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:24,840
that even a pig is better than you.

427
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:25,840
Strange, strange.

428
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:26,440
Hurt, hurt.

429
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:27,360
Come back, come back.

430
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:27,840
As a

431
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:29,600
completely lawless

432
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:30,640
psychopath,

433
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:31,360
I have decided

434
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,320
to sue and

435
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:33,920
hurt this flight attendant.

436
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:42,160
Bastard.

437
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:46,600
Actually, this case is already closed.

438
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:49,080
There's no need to cause new conflicts.

439
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:51,640
Why is this guy such a buzzkill?

440
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:52,320
So what?

441
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:52,960
No matter how powerful he is,

442
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:54,800
can he fight against all the netizens in the country?

443
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:55,960
I have to put him on the internet

444
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,680
and let him experience cyberbullying.

445
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:59,400
Otherwise, he'll really think he's something.

446
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:01,400
Yes, this video is quite satisfying.

447
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:02,800
But if it angers Hu Sheng,

448
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:04,530
and he sues you for defamation,

449
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:06,040
or if he targets Jiayi and the airline

450
00:19:06,040 --> 00:19:07,640
with more extreme actions,

451
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:09,080
how will you handle it?

452
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:10,640
You don't have to handle it anyway.

453
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:11,920
Stop worrying, okay?

454
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:16,800
Well,

455
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:20,660
just delete it.

456
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:25,960
Don't throw a tantrum.

457
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,160
Who are you giving attitude to?

458
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,640
Wait, don't delete it.

459
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:29,640
Leave it up for a night.

460
00:19:29,640 --> 00:19:31,640
Let him get the full immersive experience, right?

461
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:32,640
Yeah, yeah.

462
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:33,960
Remember to delete it tomorrow.

463
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:36,020
It makes sense to delete it tomorrow.

464
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:39,160
Come on.

465
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:40,080
Let's all join in.

466
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:41,280
Let me say a few words.

467
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:43,880
Welcome to my home, everyone.

468
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:46,920
And let's celebrate Jiayi stepping out of the shadows.

469
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:47,650
That rhymes.

470
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:49,640
What I mean is,

471
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:51,400
the main point is to eat and drink well.

472
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:52,760
Let's drink up, okay?

473
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:53,440
Okay.

474
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:54,080
Let's get together often.

475
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:54,880
Thank you all.

476
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:57,520
You really can't come up with anything better to say, huh.

477
00:19:57,520 --> 00:19:58,640
I'm just happy.

478
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:03,800
It's so nice.

479
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:06,800
It's great to see Jiayi smile again.

480
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:10,080
I feel like I've done something meaningful.

481
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:16,240
Psychological trauma doesn't heal that quickly.

482
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:17,640
I hope she finds a way

483
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:19,240
to cope with the trauma soon.

484
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:25,140
What about you?

485
00:20:26,880 --> 00:20:28,400
What way did you find?

486
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:34,640
In an uncertain life,

487
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:37,760
finding certainty.

488
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,080
So,

489
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:45,640
what you found is the law.

490
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:51,560
That's very much your style.

491
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:53,640
But don't you think

492
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:56,160
blindly pursuing this certainty

493
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:59,400
will make you lose many possibilities?

494
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:02,040
And many surprises in life

495
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:03,400
are found in these possibilities,

496
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:05,080
growing little by little.

497
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:07,280
What if it's a shock instead?

498
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:09,400
Who could be scarier than me?

499
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,560
It's just four bags of trash.

500
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:14,020
You can't bring them down?

501
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:16,210
Move around a bit after eating.

502
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:17,760
I'll go up first, Uncle.

503
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:28,400
To be honest, I don't think he's a good fit for you...

504
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:30,480
...I mean, your law firm.

505
00:21:32,880 --> 00:21:35,800
The video thing isn't as serious as you think.

506
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:37,200
It's not about the video.

507
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:39,880
You made such a big decision

508
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:41,040
to start this law firm.

509
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:43,300
You should find someone who can help you.

510
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:45,920
You don't know him.

511
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,130
Do you know him well?

512
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:53,450
Wait, I feel like someone is talking about me.

513
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:58,560
Could they be talking about me on the balcony?

514
00:21:58,560 --> 00:22:00,720
Uncle, you're overthinking it.

515
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:03,280
Who knows? What does it have to do with you?

516
00:22:03,320 --> 00:22:05,160
I'm just worried Sister Long might get fooled.

517
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:06,720
What does it have to do with me?

518
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:08,440
Lawyer Li is much more reliable than you.

519
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:10,560
They are high school classmates and childhood friends.

520
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:12,400
Childhood sweethearts, you know?

521
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:13,640
No wonder at first glance,

522
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:15,640
I thought they were a perfect match.

523
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:17,900
Their relationship is that deep?

524
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:20,560
Wanna make a bet?

525
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:22,800
What are we betting on?

526
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:23,840
Betting that

527
00:22:24,240 --> 00:22:26,680
my ragtag team can make it.

528
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:35,600
Xiaolong, I really hope you can make it.

529
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:38,160
Whether as an opponent

530
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:41,680
or as a friend.

531
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:47,680
Then I sincerely hope your wish comes true.

532
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:51,840
May my wish come true.

533
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:06,400
The candied sweet potato didn't impress them.

534
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:08,860
Next time, I'll make snowy bean paste puffs.

535
00:23:23,240 --> 00:23:24,560
What is it?

536
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:46,360
Open the door quickly. I got my internship salary.

537
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:47,160
What are you doing?

538
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:47,960
You scared me.

539
00:23:48,600 --> 00:23:49,320
Look at you.

540
00:23:49,320 --> 00:23:50,320
You're not calm at all.

541
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:52,320
It's not a big deal. Is it necessary?

542
00:24:07,600 --> 00:24:08,330
I'm leaving.

543
00:24:08,360 --> 00:24:09,490
Where are you going?

544
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:11,080
To work.

545
00:24:11,360 --> 00:24:13,220
How long are you going to lie to us?

546
00:24:13,800 --> 00:24:16,320
If we hadn't noticed something was wrong last time

547
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:17,560
and gone to your company to ask,

548
00:24:17,560 --> 00:24:20,020
were you planning to keep it from us forever?

549
00:24:25,560 --> 00:24:27,680
Hello, Director. Thank you, Director.

550
00:24:27,680 --> 00:24:29,160
Happy to get your salary, huh?

551
00:24:29,160 --> 00:24:31,800
Yes. I didn't help much with this case,

552
00:24:31,840 --> 00:24:33,000
but you still gave me money.

553
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:34,240
You can't say that.

554
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:35,960
You should get paid if you work.

555
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:36,960
Anyway, work hard,

556
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:38,800
and we'll make big money in the future.

557
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:39,960
Look at you.

558
00:24:40,320 --> 00:24:42,000
What are your orders today, Director?

559
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:44,440
You're quite eager after getting a little salary.

560
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:45,800
What do you mean eager?

561
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:46,600
Give me the bag. Come on.

562
00:24:46,600 --> 00:24:48,330
You must be tired from the trip.

563
00:24:49,360 --> 00:24:51,160
Although you didn't bring in this case,

564
00:24:51,160 --> 00:24:53,000
you also put in a lot of effort.

565
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:54,160
Anyway, in the future,

566
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:55,840
as long as you participate in a case,

567
00:24:55,840 --> 00:24:56,800
you'll get a base salary.

568
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:59,360
I must participate. I'll actively participate.

569
00:24:59,360 --> 00:25:01,080
Where's Miao? Why isn't she here yet?

570
00:25:01,080 --> 00:25:02,000
I don't know. I haven't seen her.

571
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:02,680
She probably overslept.

572
00:25:02,680 --> 00:25:03,920
Miao is never late.

573
00:25:03,920 --> 00:25:04,920
Did something happen?

574
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:05,920
Call her quickly

575
00:25:05,920 --> 00:25:07,120
and see what's wrong.

576
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:13,360
Let's not call.

577
00:25:13,360 --> 00:25:15,560
What if we interrupt something?

578
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:16,400
Right.

579
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:17,880
What could happen?

580
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:19,440
Nothing, right?

581
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:22,560
Come on, Luo Zhi, stop fidgeting.

582
00:25:22,560 --> 00:25:23,680
Come on, what is it? Tell the truth.

583
00:25:23,680 --> 00:25:25,280
Tell me everything you know.

584
00:25:26,840 --> 00:25:27,880
He doesn't know anything.

585
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:28,960
I don't know anything either.

586
00:25:28,960 --> 00:25:30,680
How could we hide anything from you?

587
00:25:30,680 --> 00:25:32,080
I'm going to the bathroom. Are you coming?

588
00:25:32,080 --> 00:25:32,360
Yes.

589
00:25:32,360 --> 00:25:32,960
Let's go.

590
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:34,220
Stand right there.

591
00:25:34,360 --> 00:25:35,160
Turn around.

592
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:37,120
Swear it.

593
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:40,200
I swear. If I'm hiding anything from you,

594
00:25:40,200 --> 00:25:41,400
Luo Zhi will fail his bar exam again.

595
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:43,440
Uncle, don't swear on this.

596
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:48,120
The family got you a good job.

597
00:25:48,320 --> 00:25:49,320
It wasn't easy.

598
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:51,000
How could you let us down?

599
00:25:51,080 --> 00:25:53,880
Miaomiao, we are doing this for your own good.

600
00:25:54,160 --> 00:25:55,640
You can't be so willful.

601
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:02,600
Miaomiao, thank you for helping me so much.

602
00:26:02,760 --> 00:26:04,440
This incident made me realize

603
00:26:04,440 --> 00:26:06,800
that life isn't just about tolerance and compromise,

604
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:08,760
but also about persistence and bravery.

605
00:26:08,760 --> 00:26:09,440
Jiayi,

606
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:11,200
your psychological evaluation report is out.

607
00:26:11,200 --> 00:26:12,400
Everything is normal.

608
00:26:12,400 --> 00:26:14,060
You can be rescheduled to fly.

609
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:19,320
No need.

610
00:26:20,200 --> 00:26:21,530
I've decided to resign.

611
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:27,330
I will try my best to find my dream-filled self again.

612
00:26:27,400 --> 00:26:29,280
I hope in the near future,

613
00:26:29,640 --> 00:26:31,500
I can return to the blue sky I love.

614
00:26:34,440 --> 00:26:35,900
You should keep it up, too.

615
00:26:36,920 --> 00:26:39,640
You are much braver than before.

616
00:26:49,080 --> 00:26:51,440
Mom, Dad.

617
00:26:54,360 --> 00:26:55,400
Growing up,

618
00:26:57,080 --> 00:26:58,480
I never had any ambitions

619
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:00,640
or persistence.

620
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:02,330
It's always been

621
00:27:02,880 --> 00:27:04,920
me doing whatever you told me to do.

622
00:27:06,920 --> 00:27:09,920
Including studying accounting and going to Honghu.

623
00:27:11,200 --> 00:27:14,600
I thought it would just go on like this.

624
00:27:15,360 --> 00:27:16,160
It was okay.

625
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:20,680
But then I met Sister Long.

626
00:27:22,400 --> 00:27:24,530
For the first time, I made my own choice

627
00:27:25,160 --> 00:27:28,560
to leave Honghu and work with Sister Long.

628
00:27:29,880 --> 00:27:31,920
During the time I worked with her,

629
00:27:33,280 --> 00:27:34,440
I finally realized

630
00:27:35,240 --> 00:27:36,000
that

631
00:27:36,880 --> 00:27:38,600
a person can live a meaningful life.

632
00:27:38,600 --> 00:27:41,440
Xiao Longnv Law Firm is reopening.

633
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:44,160
Congratulations on the opening.

634
00:27:44,160 --> 00:27:46,290
Life has something to look forward to.

635
00:27:49,560 --> 00:27:51,600
No matter how insignificant

636
00:27:52,000 --> 00:27:53,920
my efforts are,

637
00:27:55,560 --> 00:27:58,020
I can still gain my own sense of achievement.

638
00:27:59,400 --> 00:28:01,840
And I'm really lucky

639
00:28:02,040 --> 00:28:04,120
to have met such a group of partners.

640
00:28:07,440 --> 00:28:08,520
There aren't many of us,

641
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:09,360
Cheers!

642
00:28:09,360 --> 00:28:11,200
but everyone is very important.

643
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:15,460
That's also the reason why

644
00:28:18,160 --> 00:28:20,080
I must be by their side now.

645
00:28:26,320 --> 00:28:27,400
Just this once,

646
00:28:29,160 --> 00:28:30,000
okay?

647
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:32,720
Why didn't you tell me this earlier?

648
00:28:32,720 --> 00:28:34,560
No, I didn't expect it to be this fast.

649
00:28:34,560 --> 00:28:36,360
Alright, stop talking. Go drive.

650
00:28:36,360 --> 00:28:37,600
Sister Long.

651
00:28:40,120 --> 00:28:41,400
Sister Long.

652
00:28:49,440 --> 00:28:50,320
Coming.

653
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:54,440
You've got some nerve, little girl.

654
00:28:54,440 --> 00:28:56,240
You guys don't have to cover for me anymore.

655
00:28:56,240 --> 00:28:57,920
Sister Miaomiao, you're awesome.

656
00:28:57,920 --> 00:28:58,560
Of course.

657
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:01,400
Thanks, Miao.

658
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:02,600
For what, sister?

659
00:29:02,600 --> 00:29:03,600
I should be thanking you.

660
00:29:03,600 --> 00:29:06,160
I'm still waiting to be the administrative director.

661
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:07,080
You want to be the director?

662
00:29:07,080 --> 00:29:08,600
Then I should be the president.

663
00:29:08,600 --> 00:29:10,440
Uncle, law firms don't have presidents.

664
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:12,400
Why are you so obsessed with titles?

665
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:13,640
You're talking too much.

666
00:29:13,640 --> 00:29:15,170
Alright, stop blabbering.

667
00:29:15,360 --> 00:29:16,600
Let's get to work, Director.

668
00:29:16,600 --> 00:29:17,160
Let's go.

669
00:29:17,480 --> 00:29:18,600
Let's go, President.

670
00:29:18,600 --> 00:29:19,960
Can't I lead you anymore?

671
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:20,680
No, no.

672
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:21,760
Whose man are you?

673
00:29:21,760 --> 00:29:22,640
I am my uncle's...

674
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:23,440
I am Uncle Hu's man.

675
00:29:23,440 --> 00:29:25,170
You must tattoo it on your body.

676
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:26,960
Uncle Hu's man.

677
00:29:32,800 --> 00:29:35,560
This is a 1.8-liter naturally aspirated engine

678
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:36,000
with a CVT

679
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:36,920
gearbox.

680
00:29:37,160 --> 00:29:39,600
It's super fuel-efficient to drive.

681
00:29:40,600 --> 00:29:40,880
This one.

682
00:29:40,880 --> 00:29:43,640
Look, this is a premium one-owner car.

683
00:29:43,720 --> 00:29:45,000
Look at all the glass,

684
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:46,530
including the headlights.

685
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:47,640
They are all original.

686
00:29:47,640 --> 00:29:48,920
They all come with inspection reports.

687
00:29:48,920 --> 00:29:49,600
Xiao Jun,

688
00:29:49,600 --> 00:29:51,080
all these vehicles of yours,

689
00:29:51,080 --> 00:29:52,960
every single one is from a legitimate source, right?

690
00:29:52,960 --> 00:29:55,200
No smuggled or stolen cars or anything?

691
00:29:55,200 --> 00:29:58,400
Why does your occupational disease keep acting up irregularly?

692
00:29:58,400 --> 00:30:00,920
Are you here to see me or to investigate a case?

693
00:30:00,920 --> 00:30:01,800
Stay vigilant.

694
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:02,960
It's for your own good.

695
00:30:02,960 --> 00:30:04,560
If you happen to have a problematic car,

696
00:30:04,560 --> 00:30:06,360
you'll be implicated, you know?

697
00:30:06,560 --> 00:30:08,200
Just put your mind at ease

698
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:09,480
and relax.

699
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:11,480
All the cars in here

700
00:30:11,480 --> 00:30:13,920
are 100% absolutely from regular channels.

701
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:14,920
My good intentions

702
00:30:14,920 --> 00:30:16,520
are treated like dirt by you.

703
00:30:18,440 --> 00:30:19,200
Alright, I'm off work.

704
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:19,920
Come with me.

705
00:30:19,920 --> 00:30:20,800
Where to?

706
00:30:20,880 --> 00:30:22,120
Why ask so many questions?

707
00:30:22,120 --> 00:30:23,450
I can't sell you anyway.

708
00:30:23,480 --> 00:30:25,010
Even if I did, who would buy?

709
00:30:26,880 --> 00:30:28,440
What's wrong with an old man like me?

710
00:30:28,440 --> 00:30:30,000
I'm in high demand.

711
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:33,560
Come on, come on.

712
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:35,400
I'm here. Stand up.

713
00:30:36,800 --> 00:30:37,720
Welcome, Chief Li.

714
00:30:37,720 --> 00:30:38,560
Here, here, here.

715
00:30:38,560 --> 00:30:40,560
Welcome, a warm welcome.

716
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:42,600
What Chief Li? I'm retired.

717
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:44,640
Why so formal?

718
00:30:44,640 --> 00:30:45,120
What's this for?

719
00:30:45,120 --> 00:30:46,000
Today is the big day,

720
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:48,400
the 30th anniversary of our Eight Great Guardians.

721
00:30:48,400 --> 00:30:49,400
We have to be formal.

722
00:30:49,400 --> 00:30:50,480
You guys are celebrating your anniversary.

723
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:51,560
Why did you bring me here?

724
00:30:51,560 --> 00:30:52,200
Chief Li,

725
00:30:52,400 --> 00:30:54,640
you can't say 'anniversary' so lightly.

726
00:30:54,640 --> 00:30:55,920
It sounds like we old brothers

727
00:30:55,920 --> 00:30:57,920
were all wiped out 30 years ago.

728
00:30:58,360 --> 00:30:58,920
No, Ermao.

729
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:00,560
If it weren't for Chief Li back then,

730
00:31:00,560 --> 00:31:01,920
we might have really been wiped out.

731
00:31:01,920 --> 00:31:03,000
Exactly. The time we almost got killed.

732
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:04,120
So Chief Li is

733
00:31:04,120 --> 00:31:05,800
the most important person for our 30th anniversary.

734
00:31:05,800 --> 00:31:07,160
We have to invite him no matter what.

735
00:31:07,160 --> 00:31:07,680
Sit down. Come.

736
00:31:07,680 --> 00:31:09,200
Pour the wine. Pour the wine.

737
00:31:09,200 --> 00:31:10,400
Come, brother, let me pour it for you.

738
00:31:10,400 --> 00:31:11,000
Come, come, come.

739
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:12,640
We're sticking to the old rules today.

740
00:31:12,640 --> 00:31:15,640
Whoever can walk a straight line after drinking pays the bill.

741
00:31:15,640 --> 00:31:16,400
Cut the crap.

742
00:31:16,400 --> 00:31:18,160
I'll treat. It's my treat today.

743
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:19,120
Why do I say that?

744
00:31:19,120 --> 00:31:21,080
Because as the whole gang...

745
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:22,240
Wait, what gang?

746
00:31:23,800 --> 00:31:24,360
Team.

747
00:31:24,360 --> 00:31:25,200
Right.

748
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:26,400
As the team boss,

749
00:31:26,600 --> 00:31:28,800
I must treat you today.

750
00:31:28,800 --> 00:31:30,800
Brother, you're right about that,

751
00:31:30,800 --> 00:31:31,360
but

752
00:31:31,360 --> 00:31:33,000
can you still walk a straight line later?

753
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:34,240
I can run. I run in a straight line.

754
00:31:34,240 --> 00:31:36,560
Whether it's a straight line or a curved line,

755
00:31:36,560 --> 00:31:38,000
who among you has ever paid the bill?

756
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:40,730
Since you're the one who opened this restaurant.

757
00:31:41,480 --> 00:31:44,080
Thank you, Chief Li.

758
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:49,240
A man is also a flower,

759
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:52,600
also afraid of the wind and rain.

760
00:31:52,600 --> 00:31:58,400
Who can see the scars behind the strength?

761
00:31:58,680 --> 00:32:01,800
Men do shed tears,

762
00:32:01,960 --> 00:32:05,240
they just hide their broken hearts.

763
00:32:05,240 --> 00:32:07,640
I'd rather stand limping

764
00:32:07,680 --> 00:32:11,200
than kneel smiling.

765
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:13,240
Come on, guys.

766
00:32:13,240 --> 00:32:14,000
Alright,

767
00:32:14,240 --> 00:32:14,960
stop singing a cappella.

768
00:32:14,960 --> 00:32:15,640
I'll take you guys later

769
00:32:15,640 --> 00:32:16,360
to a KTV.

770
00:32:16,600 --> 00:32:17,800
Thank you, thank you.

771
00:32:17,800 --> 00:32:19,460
Daqing is calling me. Daqing.

772
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:20,840
Come over. Come over.

773
00:32:21,120 --> 00:32:22,720
I sent you that. Can you hear me?

774
00:32:22,720 --> 00:32:23,800
Come on.

775
00:32:23,800 --> 00:32:24,400
The few of us...

776
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:25,480
The few of us are all here.

777
00:32:25,480 --> 00:32:26,960
Chief Li and everyone are here too.

778
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:27,690
So come over.

779
00:32:27,800 --> 00:32:29,160
I'll send you the location later.

780
00:32:29,160 --> 00:32:29,640
Hello?

781
00:32:30,280 --> 00:32:30,800
Hello?

782
00:32:31,160 --> 00:32:32,890
Hello? Why aren't you talking?

783
00:32:33,400 --> 00:32:33,920
Hello?

784
00:32:35,680 --> 00:32:36,610
Someone's dead.

785
00:32:36,680 --> 00:32:38,480
Call the police quickly. So much blood.

786
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:40,000
Who are you? Hello?

787
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:41,440
Daqing, hello?

788
00:32:42,680 --> 00:32:43,400
Daqing.

789
00:32:46,720 --> 00:32:47,160
Wait,

790
00:32:47,400 --> 00:32:49,000
I think something happened.

791
00:32:58,240 --> 00:32:59,240
Get up, get up, get up.

792
00:32:59,240 --> 00:32:59,900
Don't push.

793
00:33:00,480 --> 00:33:01,720
My brother is the boss here.

794
00:33:01,720 --> 00:33:02,640
I came to take a look.

795
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:03,480
Can I go in and take a look?

796
00:33:03,480 --> 00:33:05,140
Don't go in and ruin the scene.

797
00:33:05,720 --> 00:33:07,080
Daqing, don't ruin the scene.

798
00:33:07,080 --> 00:33:07,680
Daqing.

799
00:33:07,680 --> 00:33:08,400
Calm down.

800
00:33:08,480 --> 00:33:09,610
Step back, Xiao Jun.

801
00:33:09,720 --> 00:33:10,920
Xiao Jun, calm down. Daqing.

802
00:33:10,920 --> 00:33:12,640
Step back. Don't ruin the scene.

803
00:33:12,640 --> 00:33:14,900
Xiao Jun, do you want to get into trouble?

804
00:33:15,840 --> 00:33:16,600
Calm down.

805
00:33:17,320 --> 00:33:17,920
Calm down.

806
00:33:18,920 --> 00:33:19,760
Calm down.

807
00:33:33,080 --> 00:33:33,610
Brother.

808
00:33:34,240 --> 00:33:35,300
That watch of yours

809
00:33:35,640 --> 00:33:36,600
is really cool.

810
00:33:37,400 --> 00:33:38,160
Well,

811
00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:41,000
would you dare lend it to me for a couple of days?

812
00:33:42,080 --> 00:33:43,810
Pretend I didn't say anything.

813
00:33:44,400 --> 00:33:45,920
I'll tell you one more time.

814
00:33:45,920 --> 00:33:46,920
No fighting.

815
00:33:47,920 --> 00:33:49,320
If you don't listen to me,

816
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:51,210
don't call me brother anymore.

817
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:51,920
Don't worry.

818
00:33:51,920 --> 00:33:52,920
Don't worry.

819
00:33:59,400 --> 00:34:00,860
If you like it, it's yours.

820
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:02,260
My brother is the best.

821
00:34:06,200 --> 00:34:07,240
Xiao Jun.

822
00:34:08,679 --> 00:34:11,210
These truck transportation routes in Leyang

823
00:34:11,880 --> 00:34:13,440
are almost all taken by you.

824
00:34:13,800 --> 00:34:14,639
What?

825
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:16,400
Aren't you afraid of biting off more than you can chew?

826
00:34:16,400 --> 00:34:18,920
You are the big brother of empty truck freight.

827
00:34:18,920 --> 00:34:20,440
Leyang is only so big.

828
00:34:20,440 --> 00:34:21,699
If I have offended you,

829
00:34:21,920 --> 00:34:24,159
I, Xiao Jun, apologize to you, okay?

830
00:34:24,719 --> 00:34:26,050
Let me offer you a toast.

831
00:34:26,679 --> 00:34:27,159
Cheers.

832
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:29,400
Cutting off someone's source of wealth

833
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:30,679
is like killing their parents.

834
00:34:30,679 --> 00:34:32,920
Do you think you can leave today?

835
00:34:35,120 --> 00:34:36,159
Xiao Jun.

836
00:34:36,600 --> 00:34:38,360
Do you know what you are to me?

837
00:34:42,480 --> 00:34:43,940
You are nothing but a fart.

838
00:34:45,880 --> 00:34:47,120
How dare you insult my brother!

839
00:34:47,120 --> 00:34:47,800
Get him!

840
00:34:51,600 --> 00:34:52,800
Calm down, calm down.

841
00:34:52,960 --> 00:34:54,080
Xiao Jun, Daqing.

842
00:34:54,360 --> 00:34:55,000
Daqing.

843
00:34:57,160 --> 00:34:58,160
Step back, step back.

844
00:34:58,160 --> 00:34:59,600
Don't worry, don't worry.

845
00:34:59,600 --> 00:35:00,200
Step back.

846
00:35:01,640 --> 00:35:02,320
I don't want anything else.

847
00:35:02,320 --> 00:35:03,960
I just want to know how Zhao Deqing died.

848
00:35:03,960 --> 00:35:05,480
Haven't I already told you?

849
00:35:05,480 --> 00:35:07,000
The case is under investigation.

850
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:08,160
We have no comment.

851
00:35:08,160 --> 00:35:09,240
What's the killer's name?

852
00:35:09,240 --> 00:35:09,840
Sir.

853
00:35:09,840 --> 00:35:11,680
Why don't you understand what I'm saying?

854
00:35:11,680 --> 00:35:12,480
About this,

855
00:35:12,640 --> 00:35:13,840
we can't disclose anything.

856
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:15,240
We're not prying.

857
00:35:15,880 --> 00:35:17,200
I'm just inquiring.

858
00:35:18,160 --> 00:35:18,480
Sister.

859
00:35:18,480 --> 00:35:19,200
What is it?

860
00:35:19,720 --> 00:35:20,780
Who killed Daqing?

861
00:35:21,640 --> 00:35:23,080
How did Daqing die? What happened?

862
00:35:23,080 --> 00:35:24,540
Who exactly is the killer?

863
00:35:24,840 --> 00:35:26,900
I only know the killer is Fu Xiaochen.

864
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:28,460
He's already been caught.

865
00:35:28,840 --> 00:35:30,440
Wait, is there anything else?

866
00:35:30,440 --> 00:35:32,400
No, that's all they told me.

867
00:35:32,480 --> 00:35:33,160
Listen, sister.

868
00:35:33,160 --> 00:35:33,840
You are Daqing's biological sister.

869
00:35:33,840 --> 00:35:34,720
And you are our sister too.

870
00:35:34,720 --> 00:35:35,680
Right. If you know anything,

871
00:35:35,680 --> 00:35:37,120
tell us quickly.

872
00:35:37,400 --> 00:35:38,460
Where does he live?

873
00:35:38,920 --> 00:35:40,960
Look, I haven't seen him for a long time either.

874
00:35:40,960 --> 00:35:42,480
What could I know?

875
00:35:43,800 --> 00:35:44,680
Hey, you...

876
00:35:44,680 --> 00:35:46,360
Hey, don't be afraid.

877
00:35:46,360 --> 00:35:46,960
Brother, you...

878
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:47,690
Brother Jun.

879
00:35:48,040 --> 00:35:50,200
Don't we have someone in the police department?

880
00:35:50,200 --> 00:35:50,800
Right.

881
00:35:52,120 --> 00:35:54,040
How much do you know about my brother Daqing's case?

882
00:35:54,040 --> 00:35:54,960
Tell me now.

883
00:35:55,400 --> 00:35:56,200
Tell us.

884
00:35:58,000 --> 00:35:59,040
Tell you what?

885
00:35:59,720 --> 00:36:01,360
Are you interrogating me?

886
00:36:01,360 --> 00:36:02,400
Sorry, Chief Li.

887
00:36:02,920 --> 00:36:04,650
My brother used the wrong word.

888
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:06,480
He meant to ask you to confess quickly.

889
00:36:06,480 --> 00:36:08,040
Used the wrong word?

890
00:36:08,120 --> 00:36:09,960
I think you're talking nonsense.

891
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:11,360
Zhao Deqing was killed.

892
00:36:11,360 --> 00:36:13,360
Why are you guys getting involved?

893
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:14,400
When the trial is over,

894
00:36:14,400 --> 00:36:15,720
everything will be clear, won't it?

895
00:36:15,720 --> 00:36:18,520
Yes, but don't you have an apprentice in the police department?

896
00:36:18,520 --> 00:36:19,720
Can you ask around for me?

897
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:21,600
Do you own the police department?

898
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:23,280
You think I can just ask around?

899
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:25,520
During the investigation, anyone asking about the case

900
00:36:25,520 --> 00:36:26,480
is breaking the rules.

901
00:36:26,480 --> 00:36:27,960
Make an exception this time.

902
00:36:27,960 --> 00:36:28,840
I'm begging you.

903
00:36:28,840 --> 00:36:30,960
Look, in front of all my brothers,

904
00:36:30,960 --> 00:36:31,960
I'm officially begging you.

905
00:36:31,960 --> 00:36:32,640
Right.

906
00:36:33,280 --> 00:36:34,720
Stop with the nonsense.

907
00:36:35,040 --> 00:36:37,000
Even if you kneel down, it won't work.

908
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,120
It's a matter of principle.

909
00:36:38,120 --> 00:36:39,520
You're still talking about principles?

910
00:36:39,520 --> 00:36:41,360
How many things have your bullshit principles ruined?

911
00:36:41,360 --> 00:36:43,080
Have you forgotten about Xiaoxin?

912
00:36:43,080 --> 00:36:44,680
Xiao Jun, what are you doing?

913
00:36:46,080 --> 00:36:46,920
Don't you know

914
00:36:46,920 --> 00:36:48,480
who you are?

915
00:36:48,880 --> 00:36:50,880
My brother is just anxious. He didn't mean it.

916
00:36:50,880 --> 00:36:51,810
Stay out of this.

917
00:36:52,600 --> 00:36:53,000
Take it easy.

918
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:54,200
Why is Chief Li like this?

919
00:36:54,200 --> 00:36:56,400
He got mad when I said he has principles.

920
00:36:57,920 --> 00:36:59,200
He didn't use to have this temper.

921
00:36:59,200 --> 00:36:59,880
Brother.

922
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:01,600
Brother Jun.

923
00:37:01,600 --> 00:37:03,360
My buddy sent a message.

924
00:37:03,360 --> 00:37:05,420
He said lawyers can review the files.

925
00:37:05,440 --> 00:37:07,240
Then we can figure it out, right?

926
00:37:07,400 --> 00:37:07,930
Let's go.

927
00:37:08,600 --> 00:37:09,440
Wait.

928
00:37:09,440 --> 00:37:10,360
Another message.

929
00:37:10,360 --> 00:37:12,480
We can't hire a lawyer.

930
00:37:12,480 --> 00:37:14,560
Only Daqing's relatives can hire a lawyer.

931
00:37:14,560 --> 00:37:15,920
Can you finish it in one breath?

932
00:37:15,920 --> 00:37:17,560
He sent it message by message.

933
00:37:17,560 --> 00:37:19,440
So I can only read it message by message.

934
00:37:19,440 --> 00:37:20,040
Let's go.

935
00:37:20,440 --> 00:37:21,800
Brother Xiao.

936
00:37:22,480 --> 00:37:24,600
We must find a lawyer for this.

937
00:37:24,600 --> 00:37:26,000
We have to find a lawyer.

938
00:37:26,040 --> 00:37:28,500
Only a lawyer can review the files, you know?

939
00:37:28,600 --> 00:37:30,400
That will cost a lot of money.

940
00:37:31,200 --> 00:37:32,800
Let's just forget it.

941
00:37:33,480 --> 00:37:36,540
My dad is still waiting for me at home to take care of him.

942
00:37:37,200 --> 00:37:38,200
My daughter runs the law firm.

943
00:37:38,200 --> 00:37:39,760
She won't charge you a penny.

944
00:37:39,760 --> 00:37:42,160
Your brother Daqing is like my own brother.

945
00:37:42,200 --> 00:37:43,600
You are like my own sister.

946
00:37:43,600 --> 00:37:44,600
About your brother's case.

947
00:37:44,600 --> 00:37:47,060
Don't worry. I promise I will see it through.

948
00:37:47,720 --> 00:37:48,680
I'll ask my daughter

949
00:37:48,680 --> 00:37:50,480
to review the files for us later.

950
00:37:50,480 --> 00:37:51,680
Review what files?

951
00:37:52,320 --> 00:37:53,760
It's in the investigation stage now.

952
00:37:53,760 --> 00:37:54,600
We can't review the files.

953
00:37:54,600 --> 00:37:56,800
We can only review the files during the review and prosecution stage.

954
00:37:56,800 --> 00:37:58,860
What nonsense are you talking about?

955
00:37:59,080 --> 00:38:00,360
This Ermao...

956
00:38:00,480 --> 00:38:02,360
He's too unreliable.

957
00:38:02,360 --> 00:38:03,200
He's...

958
00:38:03,680 --> 00:38:05,200
Daughter, can you look into it

959
00:38:05,200 --> 00:38:07,200
and arrange a death penalty for that guy?

960
00:38:07,200 --> 00:38:08,600
Dad, you think too highly of me.

961
00:38:08,600 --> 00:38:10,040
How can I arrange a death penalty?

962
00:38:10,040 --> 00:38:12,320
That's the job of the court and the procuratorate.

963
00:38:12,320 --> 00:38:13,250
Don't always...

964
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:14,480
Then...

965
00:38:15,360 --> 00:38:17,080
Then what can you do?

966
00:38:17,080 --> 00:38:17,800
Then I...

967
00:38:22,360 --> 00:38:24,000
For cases like this,

968
00:38:24,080 --> 00:38:25,400
as a lawyer,

969
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:29,200
I can file an incidental civil action

970
00:38:29,400 --> 00:38:31,860
and claim some compensation for the family.

971
00:38:32,200 --> 00:38:33,360
So you mean

972
00:38:33,920 --> 00:38:36,360
you can make the murderer's family pay some money?

973
00:38:36,360 --> 00:38:37,360
Yes, they have to pay.

974
00:38:37,360 --> 00:38:39,040
Just the death penalty would be letting him off too easy.

975
00:38:39,040 --> 00:38:41,320
Yes, that would be letting him off too easy.

976
00:38:41,320 --> 00:38:42,800
Is there any possibility

977
00:38:43,040 --> 00:38:45,000
to make them pay more?

978
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:46,040
They definitely have to pay more.

979
00:38:46,040 --> 00:38:47,240
Come over here.

980
00:38:48,520 --> 00:38:51,200
Then you might have to issue a letter of forgiveness.

981
00:38:51,200 --> 00:38:52,360
With a letter of forgiveness,

982
00:38:52,360 --> 00:38:55,240
you can get extra compensation for mental distress.

983
00:38:55,240 --> 00:38:56,520
If the other party gets the letter of forgiveness,

984
00:38:56,520 --> 00:38:57,680
their sentence will be reduced.

985
00:38:57,680 --> 00:39:00,080
The compensation for mental distress can be relatively higher.

986
00:39:00,080 --> 00:39:01,240
Wait, what are you talking about?

987
00:39:01,240 --> 00:39:02,400
What forgiveness?

988
00:39:02,680 --> 00:39:04,320
Xiaolong, whose side are you on?

989
00:39:04,320 --> 00:39:06,480
Wait, how high is high?

990
00:39:06,480 --> 00:39:08,680
I mean, what's the maximum we can ask for?

991
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:09,960
There is no legal limit.

992
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:12,200
It could be hundreds of thousands or even millions.

993
00:39:12,200 --> 00:39:15,200
Anyway, we should ask for as much as possible.

994
00:39:15,200 --> 00:39:15,960
Well,

995
00:39:15,960 --> 00:39:18,320
it still depends on the other party's financial ability

996
00:39:18,320 --> 00:39:19,880
and their willingness to compensate.

997
00:39:19,880 --> 00:39:20,080
Wait.

998
00:39:20,080 --> 00:39:22,200
What the hell are you two talking about?

999
00:39:22,200 --> 00:39:24,480
Someone died, and you two are doing business here?

1000
00:39:24,480 --> 00:39:25,080
No, Dad.

1001
00:39:25,080 --> 00:39:25,960
I'm working.

1002
00:39:25,960 --> 00:39:26,320
Why are you yelling?

1003
00:39:26,320 --> 00:39:27,200
What do you mean why am I yelling?

1004
00:39:27,200 --> 00:39:29,080
Is your job just about forgiveness?

1005
00:39:29,080 --> 00:39:31,320
Can murder be forgiven?

1006
00:39:31,320 --> 00:39:32,480
Zhao Deyan, let me tell you.

1007
00:39:32,480 --> 00:39:33,400
That's your own brother.

1008
00:39:33,400 --> 00:39:34,680
You can't let him down.

1009
00:39:34,760 --> 00:39:36,360
Xiao Jun, what are you doing?

1010
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:37,520
Are you threatening her?

1011
00:39:37,520 --> 00:39:38,320
So what?

1012
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:38,680
Brother Jun, let's...

1013
00:39:38,680 --> 00:39:39,760
Get out of the way. You stand there.

1014
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:41,400
So what?

1015
00:39:44,680 --> 00:39:46,010
My dad is just like this.

1016
00:39:47,440 --> 00:39:48,560
Jun, calm down.

1017
00:39:48,560 --> 00:39:49,800
Why are you arguing with her?

1018
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:51,480
She's just a kid, right?

1019
00:39:52,120 --> 00:39:52,680
Jun.

1020
00:39:52,680 --> 00:39:53,680
To be honest,

1021
00:39:54,120 --> 00:39:55,320
people as loyal as you

1022
00:39:55,320 --> 00:39:57,040
are really rare in today's society.

1023
00:39:57,040 --> 00:39:58,200
I really admire you.

1024
00:39:58,200 --> 00:39:59,800
Really, I totally understand how you feel.

1025
00:39:59,800 --> 00:40:01,320
I don't need your understanding right now,

1026
00:40:01,320 --> 00:40:02,080
you know?

1027
00:40:02,320 --> 00:40:03,680
If your brother was stabbed to death,

1028
00:40:03,680 --> 00:40:04,880
would you let the other party get a light sentence?

1029
00:40:04,880 --> 00:40:06,080
Of course not.

1030
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:07,520
I'd cut him into a thousand pieces.

1031
00:40:07,520 --> 00:40:08,760
Even that wouldn't be enough.

1032
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:09,320
See?

1033
00:40:09,480 --> 00:40:10,520
Anyone with a brain understands this.

1034
00:40:10,520 --> 00:40:12,320
Did you hear what she just said?

1035
00:40:12,320 --> 00:40:13,680
Yes, she was wrong.

1036
00:40:13,680 --> 00:40:15,080
She was biased.

1037
00:40:15,400 --> 00:40:17,320
But Jun, think about it from another angle.

1038
00:40:17,320 --> 00:40:18,520
You raised a good daughter.

1039
00:40:18,520 --> 00:40:19,520
As a lawyer,

1040
00:40:19,520 --> 00:40:20,600
she always stands

1041
00:40:20,600 --> 00:40:22,240
in her client's shoes.

1042
00:40:22,240 --> 00:40:24,840
How professional and what a good person she is.

1043
00:40:26,960 --> 00:40:27,760
Right?

1044
00:40:27,920 --> 00:40:28,850
What do you mean?

1045
00:40:29,760 --> 00:40:30,600
You two are in this together.

1046
00:40:30,600 --> 00:40:31,680
So you're helping her.

1047
00:40:31,680 --> 00:40:32,960
Look, you always misunderstand.

1048
00:40:32,960 --> 00:40:34,800
Why are you always so suspicious?

1049
00:40:34,800 --> 00:40:36,800
My stance is very neutral.

1050
00:40:36,800 --> 00:40:37,880
Neutral my ass.

1051
00:40:38,200 --> 00:40:39,760
You're just a fence-sitter.

1052
00:40:39,760 --> 00:40:40,240
Look, you always...

1053
00:40:40,240 --> 00:40:41,760
I don't have time to listen to your nonsense.

1054
00:40:41,760 --> 00:40:42,520
I'm not...

1055
00:40:42,520 --> 00:40:43,720
Look, get out of here.

1056
00:40:47,320 --> 00:40:48,680
Fine, I'll go. What are you yelling for?

1057
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:50,480
Your whole family loves to yell.

1058
00:40:55,280 --> 00:40:56,520
Xin, did you understand?

1059
00:40:56,520 --> 00:40:57,800
That's the situation.

1060
00:40:57,800 --> 00:40:59,480
If you were the lawyer,

1061
00:40:59,480 --> 00:41:01,240
how would you fight this case?

1062
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:03,540
From a lawyer's perspective,

1063
00:41:03,880 --> 00:41:06,240
I definitely have to respect the client's wishes.

1064
00:41:06,240 --> 00:41:07,960
My wish is that a life must be paid for with a life.

1065
00:41:07,960 --> 00:41:08,820
No, Godfather.

1066
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:10,340
From a legal perspective,

1067
00:41:10,680 --> 00:41:12,760
there's no such thing as a life for a life.

1068
00:41:12,760 --> 00:41:14,320
No, the point is she keeps trying to

1069
00:41:14,320 --> 00:41:17,180
use a letter of forgiveness to reduce the sentence.

1070
00:41:17,240 --> 00:41:18,840
Then from this perspective,

1071
00:41:18,880 --> 00:41:20,520
the family can refuse to issue a letter of forgiveness.

1072
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:21,080
In that case,

1073
00:41:21,080 --> 00:41:23,280
the suspect won't get a light sentence.

1074
00:41:23,760 --> 00:41:25,480
Xin, that's exactly what I was waiting to hear.

1075
00:41:25,480 --> 00:41:26,200
So,

1076
00:41:26,240 --> 00:41:28,400
I officially appoint you as my lawyer.

1077
00:41:29,360 --> 00:41:30,690
Who are you appointing?

1078
00:41:31,240 --> 00:41:32,000
You're not even a family member.

1079
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:34,800
What right do you have to appoint anyone, Xiao Jun?

1080
00:41:35,400 --> 00:41:36,400
What are you doing?

1081
00:41:36,400 --> 00:41:37,520
Worshipping him?

1082
00:41:38,520 --> 00:41:39,760
So what if I am?

1083
00:41:39,760 --> 00:41:40,080
I'll get going.

1084
00:41:40,080 --> 00:41:41,520
I'm just... Wait a minute.

1085
00:41:41,520 --> 00:41:43,050
You'll be my legal advisor.

1086
00:41:43,320 --> 00:41:44,960
What do you mean he's your legal advisor?

1087
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:46,200
Don't get involved in this.

1088
00:41:46,200 --> 00:41:47,680
Can you stop causing trouble?

1089
00:41:47,680 --> 00:41:49,080
How am I causing trouble?

1090
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:50,080
Daqing is my brother.

1091
00:41:50,080 --> 00:41:51,200
I just want to know how he died.

1092
00:41:51,200 --> 00:41:52,320
Is there a problem with that?

1093
00:41:52,320 --> 00:41:53,480
His business is my business.

1094
00:41:53,480 --> 00:41:53,960
Let me tell you,

1095
00:41:53,960 --> 00:41:54,520
I won't forgive them.

1096
00:41:54,520 --> 00:41:55,400
Don't forgive them then.

1097
00:41:55,400 --> 00:41:56,880
Take a Green Dragon Crescent Blade and go kill them.

1098
00:41:56,880 --> 00:41:57,800
Blood for blood, right?

1099
00:41:57,800 --> 00:41:58,800
You think I don't want to?

1100
00:41:58,800 --> 00:42:00,200
What are you yelling for?

1101
00:42:13,480 --> 00:42:14,940
When you left their house,

1102
00:42:15,040 --> 00:42:16,440
were they still arguing?

1103
00:42:16,960 --> 00:42:17,960
They stopped arguing.

1104
00:42:17,960 --> 00:42:19,680
They each shut their doors

1105
00:42:19,680 --> 00:42:21,010
and ignored each other.

1106
00:42:21,080 --> 00:42:23,080
That living room is totally wasted.

1107
00:42:23,800 --> 00:42:26,400
With Zhao Deqing's matter between them,

1108
00:42:26,960 --> 00:42:29,420
it'd be weird if they didn't have conflicts.

1109
00:42:29,560 --> 00:42:32,320
Uncle Xiao went to prison twice because of Zhao Deqing.

1110
00:42:32,320 --> 00:42:34,400
How could Xiaolong not hold a grudge?

1111
00:42:34,400 --> 00:42:34,880
Yeah.

1112
00:42:34,880 --> 00:42:37,080
This time Uncle Xiao argued with Xiaolong over Zhao Deqing,

1113
00:42:37,080 --> 00:42:38,680
so she must be feeling upset.

1114
00:42:38,880 --> 00:42:40,480
Old Xiao has a thick skull.

1115
00:42:40,480 --> 00:42:42,410
He won't come around anytime soon.

1116
00:42:42,760 --> 00:42:45,200
He'll probably keep causing trouble.

1117
00:42:45,200 --> 00:42:46,680
Anyway, Dad, the way I see it,

1118
00:42:46,680 --> 00:42:49,040
you should keep a close eye on Uncle Xiao when you're free.

1119
00:42:49,040 --> 00:42:49,760
You're right.

1120
00:42:49,760 --> 00:42:51,840
We're actually on the same page this time.
